@startuml
title POST /api/wallets/boost/prepare + /send — post-attributed transfer (tip) with finalization
skinparam backgroundColor #F8FBFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #294C60
skinparam sequence {
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #EAF5FF
  ParticipantBorderColor #38789E
  LifeLineBorderColor #6A92AA
  GroupBackgroundColor #FFF3E8
  GroupBorderColor #D97638
}

actor "Wallet holder" as Holder #FFD8C2
participant "WalletsApiSdk\n.boost(to, amount, postAuthorDid, ...)" as SDK #D5EAF7
participant "EmbersEvents\n(WebSocket)" as Events #E3D8F5
participant "Embers API" as API #FFC9A8
participant "WalletsService" as Domain #CDEACC
participant "F1r3node\nchain + observer" as Chain #FFE4A6

Holder -> SDK : boost(to, amount, postAuthorDid,\n  description?, postId?)

group Phase 1 — prepare (deploys nothing)
SDK -> API : POST /api/wallets/boost/prepare\n{ from, to, amount, post_author_did,\n  post_id?, description? }
API -> Domain : prepare_boost_contract
Domain -> Domain : render boost.rho\n(vault transfer plus post attribution)
Domain -> Chain : get head block index
Chain --> Domain : valid-after block number
Domain --> API : BoostResp { contract }
API --> SDK : PrepareResponse { response, token }
end

group Sign — locally
SDK -> SDK : signed = signContract(contract, privateKey)
end

group Subscribe before send
SDK -> Events : subscribeForDeploy(\n  hex(signed.sig).toLowerCase(), maxWait)
end

group Phase 2 — send
SDK -> API : POST /api/wallets/boost/send\n{ prepare_request, prepare_response,\n  request: signed, token }
API -> API : verify the echo hash binding
API -> Domain : deploy_boost_transfer
Domain -> Chain : deploy signed contract
Chain --> Domain : accepted
Domain --> API : deploy id
API --> SDK : 200 SendResp { deploy_id }
SDK --> Holder : { prepareResponse, sendResponse,\n  waitForFinalization }
end

group Finalization — observed, not returned
Chain --> Events : Finalized { deploy_id, ...,\n  node_type: Observer }
Events --> Holder : waitForFinalization resolves\n(or rejects after maxWait)
end

note over Domain #FFF0C7
A boost is a value transfer bound to a F1r3sky
post: post_author_did names the recipient's DID
and post_id the boosted post. The attribution is
recorded on chain and appears as a Boost entry
in both wallets' history.
end note
@enduml
